{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bb40e09d-b68b-4072-b945-dc3b3f05a5d9","step":{"id":"s1","script":"The chain rule finds how a change passes through two linked functions.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Chain rule intuition"},{"op":"text","id":"idea","region":"A2","content":"inside change × outside response"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bb40e09d-b68b-4072-b945-dc3b3f05a5d9","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Let the inside quantity be u, and let the output be y equals u squared.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"model","region":"left","latex":"u=x^2,\\quad y=u^2"},{"op":"text","id":"inside","anchor":{"el":"model","side":"below","gap":0.06},"content":"inside: x → u"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bb40e09d-b68b-4072-b945-dc3b3f05a5d9","step":{"id":"s3","script":"A small change in x first changes u, then that change affects y.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"flow","region":"right","content":"x \\to u \\to y"},{"op":"equation","id":"rates","anchor":{"el":"flow","side":"below","gap":0.06},"latex":"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{dy}{du}\\frac{du}{dx}"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Which two rates are multiplied?","expected_gist":"dy/du and du/dx"}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"bb40e09d-b68b-4072-b945-dc3b3f05a5d9","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Here, the outside response is two u, and the inside change is two x.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"factors","anchor":{"el":"rates","side":"below","gap":0.06},"latex":"\\frac{dy}{du}=2u,\\quad\\frac{du}{dx}=2x"},{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"factors","side":"below","gap":0.06},"latex":"\\frac{dy}{dx}=4ux=4x^3"}],"checkpoint":null}}
